      I've always been puzzled by the way NH keeps listing spells that
you've used past their limit.  How is a spell listed with an asterix
different from one totally wiped out by Maud?  I once thought these
could be restored by other than another spellbook (restore ability?
gain energy?) but this has not been my experience.

	It also seems that your spell energy points are completely
irrelevant past experience level 2.  The number of uses limit on each
spell is what limits your casting.  I would rather see energy points be
the limit.  Let a spell be cast as long as the caster can pay for it,
but let spells points be regenerated VERY slowly -- one per hundred moves,
or even let them only be regained by prayer or potions.  This would let
spellcaster classes' advantages be more apparent by letting them gain
more points per level, and make a spellbook more usefull than a wand
for those with the intelligence to use it.

